Based on the event history data, when Charlie analyzed the epoch training inconsistencies during the final crisis week (October 24, 2024), the checkpoint analysis revealed this specific technical bug:

**PyTorch DataLoader Shuffling Bug with Filtered Datasets**

The root cause was that the dataset length calculation was incorrect - it reported the full dataset size but only iterated through approximately 30% of the filtered data before resetting. The logging systems displayed "epoch complete" messages, but training actually stopped at only 0.3 epochs.

This bug caused training runs to appear successful in the logs while only processing 30% of Diana's filtered dataset, which explained why post-training RLHF runs were failing due to inconsistent model states from the incomplete multi-epoch checkpoints.
